// ====== SCENE FAILURE NET (2026-10-07) ======
// Sam, on his first step into the French of the night (Safari): "the thing
// crashes to weird code text again". That text is Harlowe's own crash page,
// which it puts up for ANY uncaught JavaScript error on the page, with the
// stack trace in a monospace box. The lost-context guard above covers a
// frame that fails to draw, but not a scene that fails while it is BUILT
// (Safari refuses a new WebGL context under pressure and three throws
// "Error creating WebGL context", or drops the context between the
// renderer and its first texture) nor an error in a room's own frame. So:
//  1. every scene build (all of them run through dssLoadPost) and the ten
//     rooms' frame loops are wrapped: a throw is logged and handed here;
//  2. a room that fails gives the passage its words back: the words panel,
//     if it exists, goes into its lost mode (every link offered, the card
//     gone); if the room never got that far, the half-built room and its
//     placeholder are removed, so the plain passage shows and the room is
//     tried again on the next visit;
